WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.230
That match was out of this world!

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.200
You should really come to one of them!

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:06.730
No way.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.130
Why should I have to go see my own son getting beaten half to death?

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.780
It'd be bad for my heart.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.990
Is that right?

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.240
Hello!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.080
Oh, what is it?

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.590
Um, I'm wondering how Ippo-san is doing.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.020
I'm worried since he took a lot of hits.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.210
I'm afraid he hasn't even
 gotten out of bed yet.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.840
He's bedridden? Now I'm really worried!

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.970
Are you a friend of his? 
Why don't you go see him?

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.340
Sure! Thanks for letting me in!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.490
When was the last time a girl came to visit him?

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.470
He <i>is</i> the national champion, after all.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.040
Girls should be flocking around him.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.790
Girls? Around Ippo?

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.850
He's Korakuen's hero!

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.070
You're the only one <i>not</i> in the know!

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.530
Hello.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.290
Coming through...

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:13.830
<i>He's all swollen!</i>

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.830
<i>All these bruises means he's fought really hard.</i>

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.340
<i>Our faces are so close!</i>

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.250
<i>Will he notice anything?</i>

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.350
Ippo-san, it's me, Nanako.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.210
<i>His round face is so adorable!</i>

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.850
<i>It's too much to handle!</i>

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.690
There's no use fighting it.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.690
Itagakimasu.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.320
What are you doing?!

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.850
“There's no use fighting it, so <i>itagakimasu</i> "?

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.780
You're Itagaki-kun's baby sister, aren't you?

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.330
It's “Nanako.” Um...

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:57.700
And you are?

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.020
Are you Ippo-san's girlfriend?

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.170
Makunouchi and I... know each other. I'm Kumi-

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.200
Yeah, already know.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.490
You're that grim reaper, Mashiba-san's, little sister.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.790
So, why are you even here, Kumi-san?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.790
“Why am I even...”?

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.890
I'm an actual nurse!

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.960
I'll show you how you <i>really</i> take care of a patient!

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.430
Right.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.560
Wring out the towel, but not too much.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.470
I did the towel thing already.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.530
Then let's check his pulse.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:31.570
Don't move him while he's sleeping!

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.460
Maintain air flow! Heart rate and temperature normal!

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.870
He's not in an emergency room.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:41.370
This is an outrage! <i>I</i> was supposed to be the first one to see him!

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.960
Nuts to you! I was here first!

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.440
Well I knew him before you did!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.960
Is that something to brag about?

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.970
Can we use our indoor voices?

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.890
Ippo-kun is trying to sleep.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.700
M-May I have your name?

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.970
Gosh, his towel is crooked.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.010
Honestly, two women can't do the job right?

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:04.970
I'm deducting points.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.100
P-Points?

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:11.400
I don't believe we've met, although I <i>have</i> seen both of you at the Hall a lot.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:15.610
Iimura Mari, age 23. I work as a sports writer.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:19.120
<i>We're only 3 years apart, yet she's a lot more sedate.</i>

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.120
<i>She told us both her name  </i>and<i> age. 
Talk about complacent!</i>

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.460
I'm Mashiba Kumi.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.840
Itagaki Nanako! I'm sixteen years old and still young!

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.250
<i>She didn't need that “young” part!</i>

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.350
So he now has three girls in there.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.630
Good going, Ippo.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.140
So which one of them is Ippo's type?

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:43.610
I think Ippo may have already
 found his sweetheart.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.440
I thought I was going to get his thoughts about the match, but that's not going to happen.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.260
So you're leaving?

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.440
By all means!

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.860
But since I'm here, I might as well look around the champion's bedroom.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.450
Found an album!

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:06.500
However, it's wrong to look through these without permission.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.630
That'll be an invasion of privacy.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.140
I'm still looking!

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.800
No fair! I want a look too!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.470
He's wearing a backpack!

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.470
This must be a sports festival.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.050
He's all the way at the end.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.560
He's still cute!

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.750
Who'd believe this boy would become a champion?

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:34.980
Even I'm surprised!

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.150
<i>Why are you two palling around?</i>

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.990
<i>I'm deducting points from both of you!</i>

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.330
Ippo-san looks so manly in the ring, yet so adorable when out of it!

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.830
There's no woman who's immune to that contrast.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.580
Y-You're so right!

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.380
<i>Nanako-chan is so cute and cheerful.</i>

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.670
<i>Mari-san is beautiful and more grown up.</i>

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:58.880
<i>What about me?</i>

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.510
<i>I still have a huge albatross around my neck.</i>

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:08.320
It looks like this is the first time either of you has set foot into his room.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.560
Yes, meaning?

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:13.940
It means that neither of you are in a relationship with him yet.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.600
I've always had a front-row seat
 to his training and matches.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.450
My intention is to view him as just news material.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:31.120
But when it comes to Makunouchi Ippo the boxer or Makunouchi Ippo the man...

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.130
I've recently found myself not
 entirely sure who I'm covering.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.950
You heard what she said! What are we going to do?!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.130
H-Hold on!

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.760
I-I know!

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.770
I propose we leave his care to me, since I'm a nurse.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.780
You're telling us to get lost, aren't you?

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.480
I see. So you're keeping him for yourself?

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.880
I didn't mean it like <i>that.</i>

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.880
You should be the one leaving, Kumi-san!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.770
But <i>I'm</i> an actual nurse!

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:05.230
I'm here for news coverage.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.280
Nanako-chan, you got what you came for!

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.900
No! I'm not leaving!

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.500
{overlap}Th-This is getting out of hand.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.860
You two need to leave!

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.690
{overlap}No way.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.410
No! No! No!

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:18.300
Ladies, why don't you have some tea?

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.510
All that yelling must have made you thirsty.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:21.780
Uh, sure.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.520
I-Itagakimasu.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.010
I-I've just lost points.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.420
I guess I should be happy about all this.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.310
I may baby him a lot, but I'm proud to be his mother.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.660
He's drawn a lot of attention ever since he started boxing.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.820
But I'm not proud of his physical strength.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.830
I'm proud because he's such a nice boy, which is all I can hope for.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:53.720
I get worried sick even when he tells me he's just going to practice.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.460
And now he comes back with his face this swollen.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:02.140
Boxing is what makes him get out of bed every morning, so I can't ask him to quit.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:04.470
But, at the very least...

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.470
I want to give him some time

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.380
to rest up in peace.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.030
Oh, Ippo.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:26.630
Umezawa-kun.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:30.240
Man, you should've seen the fight that happened while you were sleeping.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.750
A fight? Between who? Who won?

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.250
Was it won by KO? Decision?

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:37.090
I-I think it was won on grace and style points.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.890
I'm finally able to move around.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.900
I bet everyone at the gym is training hard.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.940
There's Itagaki-kun's rookie title matches and Takamura-san's title defense.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:56.890
But first up is...

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.440
Aoki-san's first attempt at the national title!

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:03.440
Hello!

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:05.360
Oh, Senpai!

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.400
Itagaki-kun, how are you feeling?

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.070
Never been better!

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.790
Ippo, you're here?

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.700
Shouldn't you be sleeping at home, you feeb?

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:15.700
I'm still having trouble keeping my head up.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.590
<i>Who's that scrawny-looking guy?</i>

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:25.420
<i>Did we get a new member while I was gone?</i>

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.590
Hey. Long time, no see.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.220
A-Aoki-san?

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:36.860
No way! What the heck happened to you?!

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.100
Please don't yell.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.480
What I did was take my weight-loss regimen too far.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:48.450
You know the guy's a walking bundle of nerves.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:53.060
And with his title match coming
 up, he lost sight of himself.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.040
Relax.  I'm a boxing veteran.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.960
I'll get my old body back by the
 time the match rolls around.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.860
This title match is my last chance, you know.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.670
So I'm betting everything on this.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.250
<i>I think he's going to lose.</i>

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:07.250
<i>He might lose.</i>

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:08.070
<i>He's gonna lose.</i>

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.570
<i>He  </i>will<i> lose.</i>

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:12.960
So how are you feeling?

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.430
Fine, thank you.

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:16.770
You sure picked a tough opponent.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.100
You still did great, kid.

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:22.440
I finally figured out something during that match.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:27.910
Now I know why you're avoiding
 a match with Miyata-kun.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.370
Shimabukuro-san beat my Dempsey Roll with concurrent hits.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.830
But if I hadn't matched his punches
 and instead took full hits...

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:48.800
I thought I was able to fight Miyata-kun once I mastered the Dempsey.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.880
<i>We'll settle this in the pro ring.{season 1, episode 1, 10:40}</i>

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:54.930
<i>You got it! In a pro ring!</i>

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:58.930
<i>I'll admit you've gotten stronger.{season 2, episode 26, 7:49}</i>

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:02.060
<i>You've even mastered your signature move, the Dempsey Roll.</i>

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:05.560
<i>But it still amounts to squat!</i>

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.280
<i>He left you behind.</i>

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:10.110
<i>And far behind at that!</i>

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.610
Miyata-kun's deadliest punch,

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:18.910
his counter... is the Dempsey
 Roll's Achilles' heel, isn't it?

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:26.060
The Dempsey works because it swings back and forth rhythmically like a pendulum.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:30.760
But because you can set a watch to it, a counterpuncher like Miyata

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:33.590
will take advantage of that timing.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:37.060
I knew you would figure that out for yourself.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:43.600
Also, you can assume all your future opponents are cognizant of that fact as well.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:50.280
The timing of those damaging mirror punches must have turned on a collective light bulb among them.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:54.720
The Dempsey Roll's weakness was exposed to the public the other night.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.530
I know.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:59.530
Come now, guys!

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:04.400
The match is still fresh in our minds. Let's save this talk for later.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.960
Okay. I'll see you later.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:09.540
A-Actually...

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:10.960
What?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.540
That's not all I figured out.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.960
I know the Dempsey has its weakness,

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.470
but I'm not that dismayed over it.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.520
That last match was really hard on me.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:28.550
But I'm still here, and my next matches will be just as hard, if not more.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:32.690
You think you'll still remain standing? Don't be naïve.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:38.030
You'll still train me hard, Coach.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.870
And you'll be there to cheer me on, Yagi-san.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.760
I never would have gotten here if I had relied on my own strength.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.370
But a lot of people are lending me their strength.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.000
Then, and now,

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.880
and from here on out!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.030
I thought he'd be more disheartened.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:05.150
But instead he's upbeat and looking to stay on top.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:07.690
Ippo-kun has sure grown.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.790
I'm home!

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.750
I guess I have the physical strength, but I'm nowhere near as strong as my dad.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:25.850
So I'm going to get even stronger.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:30.040
In order to go where I promised to go.

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:39.450
Great, nothing wrong here. I've recovered.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:40.760
I can even do some sparring.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:44.260
Time to go help Aoki-san!

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.230
A-Aoki-san?

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:53.370
No way!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.550
Yeah, I was trying to put on a little weight, but...

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:59.240
You call this "a little"? Are you
 going for the sumo title?

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.070
That's what we call a “rebound.”

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:03.580
He's completely lost sight of himself.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.030
Relax, guys.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:09.160
I'm a boxing veteran. I'll get
 in shape before the match.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:13.170
This title match is my last chance, you know.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.920
So I'm betting everything on this.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:20.250
<i>I think he's going to lose.{x4}</i>

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.740
So what do you really think?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.260
Will Aoki-san win?

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:29.270
He's the underdog however you look at it.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.020
But an upset victory isn't out of the question, is it?

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:32.870
No.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.770
His opponent is an orthodox boxer who sticks to fundamentals.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:41.620
If Aoki can mess up his opponent's rhythm using his unpredictable fighting style...

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.780
Then he'll win?

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.620
Still...

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:50.490
I can see his attitude changing once he becomes a big-shot champion.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.790
But I say...

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.500
the odds are still 6 to 4 against him.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.500
Should we be glad?

00:13:58.010 --> 00:14:01.540
<i>Leaving that aside, he's very knowledgeable about the opponent.</i>

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:04.300
<i>He must have watched those videos inside and out.</i>

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:07.310
Masaru-chan! You got your old weight back!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:09.140
Yeah, thank God!

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:12.210
We'll come cheer for
 you at your title match!

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:13.140
Thanks!

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:16.890
No, thank <i>you</i> for making us such good ramen.

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:20.150
Now it's our turn to fill you up with our cheers!

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:24.080
Then hold on to your hats,
 ‘cause I'll make it a good one!

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:27.590
I'll knock him out in three... no, five rounds!

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:28.830
There it is!

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:33.750
Speaking of KO's, did you see the end of that featherweight match?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.660
Makunouchi's matches are always epic.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:39.390
They literally blow you away!

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:44.330
Masaru-chan, you belong to the same gym as Makunouchi and that world champ, Takamura Mamoru, don't you?

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.170
You must see sparks flying.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.890
Yeah, I sure do.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:52.320
It must be great being a famous champion!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.750
I wanna get me some of that attention.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:55.620
Atta boy!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.810
Go get ‘em, Masaru-chan!

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:57.860
Yeah!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.070
<i>Famous, huh?</i>

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:08.200
<i>The man I admire has gone far beyond my reach,</i>

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.950
<i>and I've been outstripped by one of the younger boxers.</i>

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.870
<i>I want to be right there with them.</i>

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.910
<i>I don't want to  { \i0}just<i> be famous.</i></i>

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:21.090
<i>I want to leave behind proof that I've accomplished something in my beloved world of boxing.</i>

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:27.500
<i>I can do it! I can get that belt!</i>

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:30.320
<i>But the champion is pretty tough.</i>

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.200
<i>No, I can do it!</i>

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.060
<i>But I'm scared!</i>

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:36.190
<i>No, don't be scared!</i>

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:46.910
Don't get into an accident!

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:50.300
I need to be in one piece for my match!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.790
Shut up before I run you into a truck!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:57.240
Christ, get a room!

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:58.590
Let's jet, Kimura!

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.290
Don't order me around!

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:04.130
<i>We used to think we were invincible.</i>

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.760
<i>That everything would go our way.</i>

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:12.430
<i>But we discovered boxing
 and put that crap behind us.</i>

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:16.070
<i>We ran, ran, and ran some more.</i>

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:20.050
<i>But we still weren't winning. 
Our dreams were still unreachable.</i>

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:26.100
<i>We lost some, won some, then got taken 
back down to earth... over and over again.</i>

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.450
<i>Always missing it by  </i>that <i>much.</i>

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:30.480
<i>But this time...</i>

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.660
<i>Right, Aoki?</i>

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:43.120
I've known it for a long time.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.170
What?

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:49.450
Takamura-san is certainly a given, but even Ippo is made of better stuff than me.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:53.660
He knows how to turn it around in a huge match.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.970
That shrinking violet's got a lot of heart.

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:59.330
I may act tough, but I'm really a coward.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.890
Like a dog who's all bark but no bite.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:07.990
Ippo may have his natural strength, but he really busted his ass to get to where he is.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.130
When he outstripped me,

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:14.200
I didn't want to admit it, but I knew he could do it.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.260
But I've done it six years running,

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.980
gritting my teeth all along the way.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.880
There's nothing I can't do!

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:27.380
I'm getting that national title!

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:33.450
Once I become the champion, Kimura...

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.680
treat me like a boss.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.440
This is what I get for letting you flap your gums!

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:40.930
Watch your mouth around me!

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:41.830
Shut up!

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:42.730
Stop it!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:44.230
Lose the damn match, dumbass!

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.990
Are the tickets sold out?

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:48.780
Yeah.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:51.300
Korakuen Hall will be packed.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.910
You couldn't attract fans because they say you're too boring and professional.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:59.130
But now you can show a big crowd what you're really made of, Imae.

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:02.040
You said the same thing when
 you had me play dress-up.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.860
I'm never doing that again.

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:06.850
Nor am I putting on a show in the ring.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.750
I will quickly shut him down.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:13.100
If you KO a crazy boxer, it'll raise your stock.

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.550
KO? That's already a given.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.890
I will also thoroughly humiliate him.

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:19.960
Aoki Masaru.

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:22.980
10-6 with six KO's.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:25.440
His fighting style is impossible to pin down.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.730
His special move is the Frog Punch?

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:34.660
After completely dodging a hook, he throws an upper with his entire body.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.460
I have his timing down.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.660
I will squash that frog of his.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:44.420
If he throws a double punch, I'll just counter one of them.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:49.680
His Tailspin Corkscrew is just him twisting his body in the opposite direction of his spinning punch.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:51.990
So it's just a normal straight in the end.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.470
What about this?

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.330
Playing possum.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.520
He makes his opponents think he's down, then rises up to knock them out.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:00.100
He could win the Oscars.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.100
H-Here I am...

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.260
Here I am throwing my entire self into boxing!

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:10.120
I wanted to feel the heavy tension and the gratification of winning a match!

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.820
I've broken it off with women and even quit my job, just to devote myself to boxing!

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:16.180
I'm not going to lose.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:19.930
I'm not going to let <i>him</i> take away my belt!

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:25.000
I'm glad I passed the weigh-in.

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:28.550
The rookie title matches are about to begin.

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:31.130
It wouldn't look good if I failed the weigh-in.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:35.130
I'm really worried about Aoki-kun and his yo-yoing weight.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.540
That's the champion, Imae-kun.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.350
That man looks really dignified.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:49.910
Are we clear, Imae?

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.670
Don't get emotional in front of the challenger.

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:53.730
I get it.
